 "title": "An entry that is a page",
 "caption": "A large form is a page of its own, and the page is one container: its title in its header, its sections as the parts of its content, each with its own title and a line above it, and its actions in its footer. The sections are parts of one form that is saved once, so they are not containers of their own, and no list of the sections stands beside it. Each field is drawn as the form field of the design system lays it out: its title; the mark of its help at the end of the title's line, where the field has one; its control, as wide as its place; and one line under the control, which is its description, or its error where the value is refused; the room of that line is kept where a field has neither, so a form does not change its height when an error shows. A title never stands beside its control. Fields that are short and belong together share a row at a desktop, and on a phone each takes a row. The actions stand at the start of the footer.",
